<title>USA: N.J. governor to announce plan for school funding.</title>
<headline>N.J. governor to announce plan for school funding.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey Gov. Christine Whitman scheduled an announcement for noon Tuesday to detail how she will respond to a recent court ruling ordering more money be spent on public schools in the state.</p>
<p>The state Supreme Court earlier this month rejected Whitman's previous plan to equalize spending between rich and poor districts.</p>
<p>The ruling means the state may have to find as much as $250 million more in the fiscal 1998 budget to pay for education.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
